+---
+title: Troubleshooting
+description: Diagnose the active profile, trust, reasoning and local runtime.
+---
+
+Run `/doctor`, `/model list` and `/config list` to inspect the active profile, upstream model, protocol, source and reload policy. Diagnostics are redacted.
+
+| Symptom | Action |
+|---|---|
+| Profile does not exist | Select a saved profile ID, not an upstream model name |
+| Several profiles with no default | Set `model` or EASY_AGENT_PROFILE |
+| No model configured | Run `eagent --login` or add a complete profile; configuration editing still works |
+| Missing credential reference | Set the explicitly named variable before creating the runtime |
+| Helper failed | Fix that profile's command; no other source is borrowed |
+| Unauthenticated local server | Explicitly set authentication.type=none and omit apiKey |
+| Migration conflict | Preview, resolve different legacy keys or duplicate authentication, then apply |
+| Unsupported reasoning | Declare verified capabilities or use reasoning.mode=auto/off |
+| Unknown context/price | Supply verified capability metadata; unknown values are not Claude defaults |
+| Changed environment has no effect | Rebuild the runtime |
+| Project hooks/MCP/settings ignored | Check workspace trust; project permission mode remains restricted |
+| Unknown cache fields | Disable supported cache features with EASY_AGENT_DISABLE_PROMPT_CACHING |
+| Headless permission denied | Configure allow rules; deny still wins |
+| Sandbox blocks all commands | Check `/doctor` for OS dependencies and namespaces |
+
+Never include API Keys, `.env` content or private prompts in an issue. Check unknown fields against the [profile contract](/en/docs/config/model-profiles) and restart the runtime after changing its environment.
